[2026-10-11 15:03:48 +   538s] design notes:
    **DESIGN NOTES** (conflicts resolved: newest wins)
    1. No second factor and no identity questions. The 28 Sep and 8 Oct mails say the drawing's "second factor" box was never built.
    2. Silence (7 Oct): two short re-asks, then "Sesinizi alamadığım için görüşmeyi sonlandırıyorum." and the call ends. It does not go to the main menu, as the 2 Sep draft said.
    3. Out-of-scope questions (7 Oct): the agent first asks "Size bu konuda yardımcı olamıyorum. Sizi ana menüye aktarmamı ister misiniz?". It does not send the caller to the main menu straight away, as the 8 Oct doc still says.
    4. Three failed tries: "Size şu anda yardımcı olamıyorum. Sizi ana menüye aktarıyorum." A request to repeat something is not a failed try.
    5. Angry caller: up to three calming replies, then agent (9 Oct correction). The 2 Sep draft said 1; Deniz's 9 Oct recap said 2.
    6. Duplicate cards: same name → ask last 4, then last 6, then full number (7 Oct). Matching is done in a code hook, never by the model.
    7. The agent never says more than the last four digits (9 Oct). The masked list is never shown to the model.
    8. Currency names are always spoken in full: Türk Lirası, Dolar, Euro, İngiliz Sterlini. Never codes, never "Sterlin" (7 and 10 Oct). A missing currency block is left out of the no-debt sentence.
    9. Multi-card callers are asked the other-card question before the offer (10 Oct). A no-debt reading has no offer: other-card question or main menu (Selin 10 Oct, "as in my document").
    10. Card with no statement cut yet: "Kartınızın henüz kesilmiş bir ekstresi olmadığı için ..." plus the first cut date only if the service gave one (10 Oct).
    11. Cut day: the 00.00 sentence first, then totalDebt per currency (10 Oct). After the due date: say it passed, then the totals, then the auto-payment remainder if there is one.
    12. Statement week: once per calendar year (7 Oct), not the IVR's "ayda bir / yılda üç". No pre-check service exists, so the change is always offered, with the optional limit line. STW-091/092 are not used.
    13. Joint-statement warning comes after the new dates and before "Onaylıyor musunuz?" (Elçin, 7 Oct).
    14. E-mail goes only to the registered address and only the latest statement. Long addresses are shortened. The FAQ's "any address" is overridden by the 29 Sep mail.
    15. Service errors go to an agent with the bank's sentence, including the week sentence. The cards.list 404 "no card" is not a failure; it goes to the main menu.
    16. Third-party card: security sentence and back to the menu/login, with nothing disclosed (8 Oct §8.6 and the examples).
    17. Amounts and dates are pre-formatted in code. The model reads fixed TTS text built from the tool data and never computes figures.
